    "explanation": "This ruling is addressed to both parties. The dispute is a route deviation, and the platform's own trace decides it.\n\nTHE DEVIATION IS ESTABLISHED. The GPS trace (EV-GPS-02818) measures the drive between the recorded pickup and drop-off at 14.44 km against the booked optimal route of 12.0 km (EV-TRIP-02818, optimal_route_source routing-engine-v3.2). That is an excess of 2.44 km, or 20.33% of optimal. Under POL-RD-01 the trace figure governs and the trip record's rounded 14.4 km copy may not be cited for the threshold test. Both limbs pass: the excess is greater than 0.8 km and greater than 20% of optimal. The deviation is therefore established, but it is NOT material (2.44 km is below the 8.0 km figure and 20.33% is below the 50% figure).\n\nTHE TRACE IS NOT IMPAIRED. It carries 114 fixes at a 10-second interval with 100.0% coverage, zero gaps and a maximum gap of 0.0 seconds, so none of POL-RD-07(a) to (c) fires, no independent corroboration is required, and POL-RD-10(3) is not engaged. It is clean both at the schema pre-pass and for policy purposes.\n\nNOTHING EXCUSES THE EXCESS. The chat log (EV-CHAT-02818) holds zero messages, so no rider-requested detour under POL-RD-04 can be made out (no instruction, no waypoint_hint, no named road). No pickup or drop-off amendment is recorded (pickup_amended_at and dropoff_amended_at are null, amended_optimal_distance_km is null), so POL-RD-05 cannot be run and the booked 12.0 km optimal stands. The trip is RYDE_X, not RYDE_POOL, so POL-RD-12 does not apply.\n\nDRIVER — YOUR TRAFFIC ASSERTION IS DISCARDED. Your counterparty statement says 'Minor detour because of a road works sign.' Under POL-RD-13 that assertion is tested against the traffic_advisory for this trip and nothing else. There is no advisory on file: EV-ADVIS-02818-01 is MISSING, weight_multiplier 0.0, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT. The POL-RD-03 comparison therefore cannot be run, POL-RD-03 is unavailable, and your assertion carries no weight under POL-RD-08. You named no advisory evidence ID, so under POL-RD-13(1) this is a gap in the bundle, not an exculpatory clause invoked against a cited artifact, and POL-RD-10(5) is NOT engaged — the case is decided on the measured excess rather than escalated. The assertion is recorded as discarded, and no amended optimal is supplied by it. The finding does not depend on the missing artifact (which can carry no fact); it rests on the weight-1.0 trace, trip record and fare ledger, so it survives.\n\nTHE REFUND IS ARITHMETIC (POL-RD-02). The fare model is METERED, not upfront, so POL-RD-02 governs instead of POL-RD-11. On separate lines: charged_total = 20.66 (EV-FARE-02818); recomputed_fare = (3.80 base + 0.75 x 12.0 km + 0.28 x 16.0 min) x 1.0 surge + 0.80 platform fee + 0 ERP + 0 fixed surcharge + 0 waiting time - 0 promo = 18.08; refund = 20.66 - 18.08 = 2.58, rounded UP to SGD 2.60. The surge multiplier of 1.0 is read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier, not from the trip record. The refund is above the SGD 0.50 de minimis floor and well short of the 90% full-refund share, so the outcome is a partial refund of SGD 2.60.\n\nNO PASS-THROUGH CORRECTION. The fare carries zero ERP gantries, zero tolls and no airport surcharge, so POL-RD-09 adds nothing; under POL-RD-09(1) any off-route ERP would in any event already be comprehended in the POL-RD-02 figure rather than added to it. No billing-integrity referral arises under POL-RD-09(4).\n\nNO DRIVER COMPENSATION AND NO CONDUCT REFERRAL. The billed distance (14.4 km) is not short of the trace (14.44 km) by more than 1.0 km, so the POL-RD-04 compensation limb does not fire. driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 1 against 188 completed trips in 90 days — below the 3-flag threshold and below the 0.05 ratio — so no POL-RD-06 repeat-pattern uplift and no POL-RD-06(c) conduct referral follow. The rider profile shows no POL-RD-08 corroboration hurdle. Both profiles were used only for the tests that name them; no other profile field grounded any finding (POL-GEN-01).\n\nEXECUTION. The monetary effect of SGD 2.60 is at or below the SGD 8.00 execution threshold, so it executes on issue, subject to the appeal route under POL-GEN-04. The driver's assertion that a road works sign caused the detour was discarded for want of any advisory on file."
